To Solve this problem we have 3 approaches 
BRUTE FORCE APPROACH:NESTED LOOPS
BETTER APPROACH:HASH SET
OPTIMAL APPROACH:SORTING + TWO POINTERS

Core Pattern:
Sort the array
      ↓
Fix one element i
      ↓
j = i + 1
k = len(n) - 1
      ↓
while j < k
      ↓
sum = n[i] + n[j] + n[k]
      ↓
┌──────────────┬──────────────┬──────────────┐
│ sum < 0      │ sum > 0      │ sum == 0     │
│ j++          │ k--          │ found        │
└──────────────┴──────────────┴──────────────┘
                                      ↓
                              move j and k
                                      ↓
                              skip duplicates
                                      ↓
                               next i


BRUTE FORCE APPROACH:
-----------------------------------
n = list(map(int, input().split()))
n.sort()
result = []
for i in range(len(n)):
    for j in range(i + 1, len(n)):
        for k in range(j + 1, len(n)):
            if n[i] + n[j] + n[k] == 0:
                triplet = (n[i], n[j], n[k])
             if triplet not in result:
                    result.append(triplet)
print(result)

TC:O(n³)
SC:O(1)



BETTER APPROACH:
----------------------------------------------
n = list(map(int, input().split()))
result = set()
for i in range(len(n)):
    seen = set()
    for j in range(i + 1, len(n)):
        target = -n[i] - n[j]
        if target in seen:
            triplet = tuple(sorted([n[i], n[j], target]))
            result.add(triplet)
        seen.add(n[j])
print(result)

TC:O(n²)
SC:O(n)


OPTIMAL APPROACH:
----------------------------------------------------
n = list(map(int, input().split()))

n.sort()
result = []

for i in range(len(n)):
    if i > 0 and n[i] == n[i - 1]:
        continue
    j = i + 1
    k = len(n) - 1
    while j < k:

        total = n[i] + n[j] + n[k]

        if total < 0:
            j += 1

        elif total > 0:
            k -= 1

        else:
            result.append([n[i], n[j], n[k]])

            j += 1
            k -= 1

            while j < k and n[j] == n[j - 1]:
                j += 1

            while j < k and n[k] == n[k + 1]:
                k -= 1

print(result)

TC:O(n²)
SC:0(1)
